<!-- Page header -->
<header class="lp-page-head">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 820px;">
            <div class="lp-eyebrow">Agents &middot; RAG &middot; code graph</div>
            <h1 class="lp-h2" style="font-size: clamp(40px, 5.2vw, 64px);">Soli is built <span class="lp-em">for AI.</span></h1>
            <p class="lp-lead">
                Soli gives coding agents what it gives you: one way to do each thing, a short language, and a
                complete product stack. Code that agents write in few tokens and humans can review, from
                <code>soli new</code> to production, the LLM and the retrieval layer included.
            </p>
            <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 14px; margin-top: 8px;">
                <a href="/docs/development-tools/ai-agents" class="lp-btn lp-btn-solid">Agent setup</a>
                <a href="/docs/builtins/ai" class="lp-btn lp-btn-line">LLM &amp; embeddings</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</header>

<!-- Principles -->
<section class="lp-section" style="background: var(--paper-sunk);">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 760px;">
            <div class="lp-eyebrow">Why it works</div>
            <h2 class="lp-h2">A small language with a map</h2>
            <p class="lp-lead">An agent does best where there is one obvious next file and a fast way to know it got it right.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="lp-grid-2" style="margin-top: 56px;">
            <div class="lp-card">
                <span class="lp-num">01</span>
                <h3 class="lp-h3">Convention over configuration</h3>
                <p><strong>Soli gives agents a map.</strong> One folder for models, one for controllers, one for jobs. <code>resources("posts")</code>, <code>soli generate scaffold</code> and a root <code>CLAUDE.md</code>, so a generated change lands close to idiomatic Soli with less prompting.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lp-card">
                <span class="lp-num">02</span>
                <h3 class="lp-h3">Token efficiency</h3>
                <p><strong>Less language means more context.</strong> Soli is small on purpose: postfix <code>unless</code>, implicit returns, no package manager, no bundler. Agents spend tokens on the product, not on boilerplate or five ways to import a model.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lp-card">
                <span class="lp-num">03</span>
                <h3 class="lp-h3">A contract, not a prompt</h3>
                <p><strong>Verification is not optional.</strong> Every <code>soli new</code> app ships <code>AGENTS.md</code>, per-folder guides, <code>/soli-verify</code> and a coverage gate. When lint or tests fail, the rule is to fix the cause, never to weaken the suite.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lp-card">
                <span class="lp-num">04</span>
                <h3 class="lp-h3">The one-person stack</h3>
                <p><strong>One person can ship more.</strong> MVC, jobs, auth, LiveView and the LLM live in one binary. Adding an agent does not mean stitching a vector database, a queue and a chat SDK together.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Agents on Soli -->
<section class="lp-section" id="agents-on-soli">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 800px; margin-bottom: 48px;">
            <div class="lp-eyebrow">Evals</div>
            <h2 class="lp-h2">Agents on Soli</h2>
            <p class="lp-lead">
                The idea behind Rails&rsquo; Agents on Rails: measure coding agents on a frozen set of small Soli tasks.
                The first board runs Claude Code (<code>claude -p</code>), OpenCode with DeepSeek, and Grok Build, graded by
                <code>soli lint</code> and <code>soli test</code>. Stage 1 only, one capability per task. It is not a
                Cursor-versus-Claude-Code table, and not Soli versus Rails on the same numbers.
            </p>
            <p class="lp-note">
                Methodology: <a href="/docs/development-tools/ai-evals" class="lp-link" style="display: inline;">Agents on Soli</a>.
                Harness <code><%= str(evals["harness"]) %></code>, <%= str(evals["runs_per_model"]) %> runs per model.
            </p>
        </div>

        <% if evals["models"].length() > 0 %>
        <div class="lp-table-wrap">
            <table id="ai-evals-table" class="lp-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th data-sort="id">Model</th>
                        <th data-sort="accuracy">Accuracy</th>
                        <th data-sort="speed_s">Median speed</th>
                        <th data-sort="tokens">Mean tokens</th>
                        <th data-sort="cost_usd">Mean cost</th>
                        <th data-sort="api_recall">API recall</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <% for row in evals["models"] %>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="lp-mono" data-v="<%= str(row["id"]) %>"><%= str(row["id"]) %></td>
                        <td data-v="<%= str(row["accuracy"]) %>"><%= str(row["accuracy"]) %></td>
                        <td data-v="<%= str(row["speed_s"]) %>"><%= str(row["speed_s"]) %>s</td>
                        <td data-v="<%= str(row["tokens"]) %>"><%= str(row["tokens"]) %></td>
                        <td data-v="<%= str(row["cost_usd"]) %>">$<%= str(row["cost_usd"]) %></td>
                        <td data-v="<%= str(row["api_recall"]) %>"><%= str(row["api_recall"]) %></td>
                    </tr>
                    <% end %>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="lp-note" style="margin-top: 16px;">Last run: <%= str(evals["generated_at"]) %>. Click a column to sort.</p>
        <script>
        (function () {
            var table = document.getElementById("ai-evals-table");
            if (!table) return;
            var tbody = table.tBodies[0];
            table.querySelectorAll("th[data-sort]").forEach(function (th, idx) {
                th.addEventListener("click", function () {
                    var rows = Array.prototype.slice.call(tbody.rows);
                    var dir = th.getAttribute("data-dir") === "asc" ? "desc" : "asc";
                    table.querySelectorAll("th").forEach(function (h) { h.removeAttribute("data-dir"); });
                    th.setAttribute("data-dir", dir);
                    rows.sort(function (a, b) {
                        var av = a.cells[idx].getAttribute("data-v") || "";
                        var bv = b.cells[idx].getAttribute("data-v") || "";
                        var an = parseFloat(av), bn = parseFloat(bv);
                        var cmp = (!isNaN(an) && !isNaN(bn)) ? (an - bn) : av.localeCompare(bv);
                        return dir === "asc" ? cmp : -cmp;
                    });
                    rows.forEach(function (r) { tbody.appendChild(r); });
                });
            });
        })();
        </script>
        <% else %>
        <div class="lp-card" style="background: transparent; border-style: dashed; border-color: var(--ink-faint); max-width: 800px;">
            <h3 class="lp-h3" style="font-size: 20px;">No numbers until the first run is committed.</h3>
            <p>
                The tasks are in <code>evals/</code> (12 of them) and the harness is <code>scripts/evals/run.py</code>.
                A paid run writes <code>www/data/ai_evals.json</code>. We will not invent scores for this table.
            </p>
        </div>
        <% end %>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Day one -->
<section class="lp-section" style="background: var(--paper-sunk);">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 48px;">
            <div class="lp-eyebrow">soli new</div>
            <h2 class="lp-h2">An agent workspace on day one</h2>
            <p class="lp-lead"><code>soli new myapp</code> writes the files Claude Code, Cursor, Aider, Copilot CLI and Codex all read.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="lp-split" style="align-items: start;">
            <div class="lp-table-wrap">
                <table class="lp-table lp-stack">
                    <thead>
                        <tr><th>Path</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td class="lp-mono">CLAUDE.md</td><td>The root guide: verification loop, footguns, recipes</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="lp-mono">AGENTS.md</td><td>A tool-agnostic pointer to that guide</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="lp-mono">app/*/CLAUDE.md</td><td>Controllers, models, views, middleware, tests, migrations</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="lp-mono">.claude/commands/</td><td><code>/soli-verify</code>, <code>/soli-test</code>, <code>/soli-resource</code></td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="lp-mono">.claude/settings.json</td><td>Safe <code>soli</code> subcommands, allowed up front</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="lp-mono">docs/</td><td>The language docs, bundled, so the agent needs no network</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="lp-code">
                <div class="lp-code-bar"><span>the loop an agent runs</span><span class="lp-tag">red means not done</span></div>
<pre><code><span class="ok">$</span> <span class="n">soli new shop</span>
<span class="c"># CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, per-folder guides, docs/</span>

<span class="ok">$</span> <span class="n">soli generate scaffold orders total:decimal</span>
<span class="ok">$</span> <span class="n">soli lint app/controllers/orders_controller.sl</span>
<span class="ok">&#10003;</span> <span class="c">no issues</span>
<span class="ok">$</span> <span class="n">soli test tests/controllers/orders_controller_spec.sl</span>
<span class="ok">&#10003;</span> <span class="c">14 tests, 0 failures</span>
<span class="ok">$</span> <span class="n">soli test --coverage --coverage-min 90</span></code></pre>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 28px; margin-top: 32px;">
            <a href="/docs/development-tools/ai-agents" class="lp-link">AI agents in Soli projects &rarr;</a>
            <a href="/docs/blog/ai-coding-agents" class="lp-link">The agent philosophy post &rarr;</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Code graph -->
<section class="lp-section" id="code-graph">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 48px;">
            <div class="lp-eyebrow">Graph RAG</div>
            <h2 class="lp-h2">A code graph your agent can query</h2>
            <p class="lp-lead">
                <code>soli graph build</code> turns your project into a graph: files, classes, models, controllers,
                methods, routes and views, joined by what connects them (a route <em>routes to</em> an action, a method
                <em>calls</em> another, an action <em>renders</em> a view). Every node is embedded. <code>soli graph query</code>
                finds the code that matches a task, then walks one hop out, so the agent gets the neighbourhood,
                not a random snippet.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="lp-split lp-split-wide" style="align-items: start;">
            <div class="lp-code">
                <div class="lp-code-bar"><span>Terminal</span><span class="lp-tag">--json for agents</span></div>
<pre><code><span class="ok">$</span> <span class="n">soli graph build</span>
<span class="c"># nodes + edges + embeddings, stored in SoliDB</span>

<span class="ok">$</span> <span class="n">soli graph query --json \</span>
    <span class="s">"where is authentication handled?"</span>
<span class="n">{</span> <span class="v">"mode"</span><span class="n">:</span> <span class="s">"semantic"</span><span class="n">, </span><span class="v">"results"</span><span class="n">: [{</span>
    <span class="v">"qualified_name"</span><span class="n">:</span> <span class="s">"SessionsController#create"</span><span class="n">,</span>
    <span class="v">"file"</span><span class="n">:</span> <span class="s">"app/controllers/sessions_controller.sl"</span><span class="n">,</span>
    <span class="v">"line"</span><span class="n">: 12, </span><span class="v">"score"</span><span class="n">: 0.82,</span>
    <span class="v">"neighbors"</span><span class="n">: [</span>
      <span class="n">{ </span><span class="v">"edge_kind"</span><span class="n">:</span> <span class="s">"routes_to"</span><span class="n">, </span><span class="v">"name"</span><span class="n">:</span> <span class="s">"POST /login"</span> <span class="n">},</span>
      <span class="n">{ </span><span class="v">"edge_kind"</span><span class="n">:</span> <span class="s">"calls"</span><span class="n">, </span><span class="v">"name"</span><span class="n">:</span> <span class="s">"User#authenticate"</span> <span class="n">},</span>
      <span class="n">{ </span><span class="v">"edge_kind"</span><span class="n">:</span> <span class="s">"renders"</span><span class="n">, </span><span class="v">"name"</span><span class="n">:</span> <span class="s">"sessions/new"</span> <span class="n">}</span>
    <span class="n">]</span>
<span class="n">}]}</span></code></pre>
            </div>

            <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;">
                <div class="lp-card">
                    <h3 class="lp-h3" style="font-size: 20px;">Always current in dev</h3>
                    <p>With an embedding key set, <code>soli serve --dev</code> reindexes on every save. It re-embeds only the nodes whose text changed, so a one-file edit costs a handful of embeddings, not thousands.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="lp-card">
                    <h3 class="lp-h3" style="font-size: 20px;">Narrow the question</h3>
                    <p><code>--path api/</code> keeps one side of a mono-repo, <code>--kind method,route</code> one kind of node, <code>--hops 2</code> walks further. Without embeddings it falls back to a weighted keyword search, so the command always answers.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="lp-card">
                    <h3 class="lp-h3" style="font-size: 20px;">Not only Soli code</h3>
                    <p>Point it at any repository and pick the file types with <code>--ext rb,erb</code>: a Rails app indexes like a Soli one. Same storage, same queries. The graph lives in SoliDB, which provides the graph and vector engines.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 28px; margin-top: 32px;">
            <a href="/docs/development-tools/graph" class="lp-link">Code graph docs &rarr;</a>
            <a href="/docs/blog/code-graph-rag" class="lp-link">Code Graph RAG, the long version &rarr;</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- AI in the product -->
<section class="lp-section lp-night">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 800px; margin-bottom: 48px;">
            <div class="lp-eyebrow">In your app</div>
            <h2 class="lp-h2">AI in the product, not a sidecar</h2>
            <p class="lp-lead">The binary that serves your app also talks to an OpenAI-compatible chat API, embeds and reranks rows, and grounds answers in your own data with <code>Model.rag</code>. No extra process.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="lp-grid-3" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
            <div class="lp-card">
                <h3 class="lp-h3" style="font-size: 20px;"><a href="/docs/builtins/ai">llm_generate</a></h3>
                <p>Chat completions with <code>SOLI_LLM_API_KEY</code>. Stream tokens with <code>out.llm_stream</code> inside <code>sse</code>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lp-card">
                <h3 class="lp-h3" style="font-size: 20px;"><a href="/docs/database/search#rag">.similar() &middot; Model.rag</a></h3>
                <p>Embed on save, retrieve by cosine or hybrid search, ground the prompt. <a href="/docs/blog/rag-product-discovery" class="lp-link" style="display: inline;">Product discovery tutorial</a>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lp-card">
                <h3 class="lp-h3" style="font-size: 20px;"><a href="/docs/builtins/ai">embed &middot; rerank</a></h3>
                <p><code>embed</code> and <code>embed_batch</code> turn text into vectors; <code>rerank</code> reorders rows against a query. OpenAI, or a self-hosted vLLM, Ollama or llama.cpp.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="lp-code">
            <div class="lp-code-bar"><span>app/controllers/search_controller.sl</span><span class="lp-tag">retrieve, then stream</span></div>
<pre><code><span class="c"># GET /search?q=… — answer from the catalogue, token by token</span>
<span class="n">hits = Product.similar(q, { </span><span class="s">"limit"</span><span class="n">: 8 })</span>
<span class="n">context = hits.map { |hit| hit.name }.join(</span><span class="s">"\n"</span><span class="n">)</span>
<span class="n">out.llm_stream(</span>
  <span class="s">"Answer only from the catalogue."</span><span class="n">,</span>
  <span class="s">"Question: #&#123;q}\n\nContext:\n#&#123;context}"</span>
<span class="n">)</span></code></pre>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Why agents do well -->
<section class="lp-section">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 48px;">
            <h2 class="lp-h2">Why agents do well here</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-split" style="align-items: start;">
            <blockquote class="lp-quote">
                Convention over configuration is not nostalgia. It is a prior. One MVC layout, one test DSL, one job
                folder, one <code>CLAUDE.md</code>: the model already knows the shape of the next file.
            </blockquote>
            <blockquote class="lp-quote">
                A fast <code>soli test</code> loop is the difference between an agent that guesses and an agent that
                finishes. If it is red, it is not done.
            </blockquote>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section style="padding-bottom: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px);">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
        <div class="lp-cta">
            <h2 class="lp-h2">Give your agent a map.</h2>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px;">Install Soli, run <code style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;">soli new</code>, and point your agent at the folder.</p>
            <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 14px;">
                <a href="/docs/getting-started/installation" class="lp-btn lp-btn-solid">Install Soli</a>
                <a href="/docs/blog/ai-coding-agents" class="lp-btn lp-btn-line">Read the long version</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
